cryptoauthlib 3.7.9: bound how long one kit transfer can block on a tap pad
that stopped answering, since callers hold the tap pad lock across it.

Apply AFTER cryptoauthlib-tappad-lock.patch. The first non-NUL byte (tty) or
report (HID) of a reply may take 2.5 s, each later one 0.5 s, and the whole
reply 3 s from the command's first byte; a tty write waits at most 1 s for
room. Input left from an earlier command is drained before a new one is sent.
A failed tty transfer discards pending output and closes the tty. A HID device
whose first wait for a reply timed out gets only the 0.5 s wait until it
answers again. Kit UART: at most 64 leading NULs are skipped per receive.
See README-tappad-lock.md next to this file.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/hal/hal_bounded_io.h
